From da3209adedac478d5eeda5dbfd222df5f0ec99a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John R Reeves III <johnreevesiii@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 08:35:50 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 18/22] rec-wasm: add JIT self-test and clock jitter test hooks

fly_jit_selftest() checks, in a booted core, fly_block_idle_ff on SH4
self-loops decoded by the real decoder (pure poll and bare wait must
qualify; a poll with a dt timeout, a calibration counter, static
loops with a store or a counter, and polls with pref or a store must
not) and that an or.b #imm,@(R0,GBR) store through wasm_exec_ifb bumps
the written page's generation, with a control that the bare
interpreter handler does not. It borrows and restores the last 4 KB of
RAM. Driven by host/tools/jit-selftest.mjs.

fly_test_clock_jitter(seed, max_us) adds a seeded, growing
pseudo-random skew to the JIT's wall clock. Every budget and timing
read in rec_wasm.cpp now goes through fly_now(), which is
emscripten_get_now() while the hook is off (the default). With
different seeds mode 0's budgets decide differently and the guest
diverges; mode 1 must not (host/tools/det-jitter-test.mjs).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
